// ============================================================================
// [P2.2d-C1] Circuit 1 (denominated pool commitment): trace_length = 128.
// 6 periodic columns bind all 4 transition constraints via DEEP-ALI at a
// single OOD point z, closing the P2.2d soundness gap:
//   1. The legacy generic quotient (`compute_quotient_at_position_generic`)
//      only bound Poseidon on cycle 0 — cycles 1 and 2 (epoch_hash, commitment)
//      were unconstrained except via per-query trace-aligned checks.
//   2. The chain constraint `next[1]@row64 = current[0]@row63` (cycle 1's
//      output = cycle 2's right input = epoch_hash) was never enforced anywhere
//      on-chain.
//
// Layout:
//   C1_RC0/RC1/RC2:        Poseidon t=3 round constants within each hash cycle
//                          (pos_in_cycle in 0..29, cycles 0..2 active).
//   C1_ROUND_FLAG:         1 on active Poseidon rounds, 0 on cycle boundary /
//                          padding rows (96..127).
//   C1_CHAIN_FLAG:         1 at row 63 only (boundary of cycle 1 → cycle 2
//                          input chaining for epoch_hash).
//   C1_IS_BOUNDARY:        1 at last row of each active cycle (rows 31, 63,
//                          95) — allows free transitions.
//
// Regenerate with:
//   cargo test -p p01-stark --lib emit_circuit_1_periodic_coeffs -- --ignored --nocapture
// ============================================================================

